From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: ROG5 log INTF underruns with the mode and core clock

An INTF underrun on the DP side only incremented a debugfs counter (and took
a devcoredump snapshot on the first one). The counter also stops while the
video encoder's IRQs are off after the idle timeout (ENTER_IDLE ->
_dpu_encoder_irq_disable), so a monitor showing the underflow colour on
every frame looked like a "latched" underrun (2026-09-29/30, MSI 491C at
5120x1440@60 and 3840x1080@100: 16151 underruns in 178 s, then no change
while the desktop was idle).

Log the 1st, 2nd, 4th, ... 1024th underrun after each enable and every
1024th after that, with the mode, pixel clock and the core clock in effect.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -1491,16 +1491,34 @@
 void dpu_encoder_underrun_callback(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc,
 		struct dpu_encoder_phys *phy_enc)
 {
+	int cnt;
+
 	if (!phy_enc)
 		return;
 
 	DPU_ATRACE_BEGIN("encoder_underrun_callback");
-	atomic_inc(&phy_enc->underrun_cnt);
+	cnt = atomic_inc_return(&phy_enc->underrun_cnt);
 
 	/* trigger dump only on the first underrun */
-	if (atomic_read(&phy_enc->underrun_cnt) == 1)
+	if (cnt == 1)
 		msm_disp_snapshot_state(drm_enc->dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * ROG5: underruns were only visible as a debugfs counter, which also
+	 * stops while the encoder IRQs are off after the idle timeout, so a
+	 * blue (underflow colour) DP monitor looked "latched". Say it in the
+	 * log, with what the rate depends on: 1, 2, 4, ... 1024, then every
+	 * 1024th since this enable.
+	 */
+	if (is_power_of_2(cnt) || !(cnt % 1024))
+		dev_info_ratelimited(drm_enc->dev->dev,
+			"INTF_%d underrun #%d: %dx%d@%d pclk %d kHz, core clk %llu Hz\n",
+			phy_enc->hw_intf ? phy_enc->hw_intf->idx - INTF_0 : -1, cnt,
+			phy_enc->cached_mode.hdisplay, phy_enc->cached_mode.vdisplay,
+			drm_mode_vrefresh(&phy_enc->cached_mode),
+			phy_enc->cached_mode.clock,
+			phy_enc->dpu_kms->perf.core_clk_rate);
+
 	trace_dpu_enc_underrun_cb(DRMID(drm_enc),
 				  atomic_read(&phy_enc->underrun_cnt));
 	DPU_ATRACE_END("encoder_underrun_callback");
